  {
    "number": 3,
    "title": "docs: refine complete studio-content law planning",
    "body": "The existing FT-000B card does not yet specify all contextual studio-content laws and proof obligations retained by [Calliope issue9](https://github.com/octave-commons/calliope/issues/9). This planning PR appends the complete eleven original invariants and six proof requirements to that same card and adds a criterion-to-law/test design contract.\n\nThe proposal covers distinct work/render/clip/arrangement/export identities, immutable render references, contextual clip ranges and fade sums, deterministic accepted-clip arrangements, complete export identity, scoped ratings, explicit marker epistemic tiers, and closed non-executable smart-list programs. Labels/dispositions, ordered playlists and attention workspaces remain in the full outcome. Future implementation must supply meaningful positive/negative/property fixtures, independent JVM/CLJS pure-law execution, hosted counts, zero-warning lint, namespace audit and revision-bound Receipt River proof.\n\nThe original card prefix, UUID, frontmatter, five-point estimate, breakdown state, dependency on human-owned incoming FT-000A and Rheos event history remain byte-exact. Historical APPROVE AFTER CHANGE concerns the recorded design disposition; it supplies neither readiness nor approval of this new plan. Review must assess the full estimate/scope before any lawful Rheos admission. No decomposition or implementation is included.\n\nThe inherited release/publication scope remains intact and open. This proposal specifies the complete issue9 content outcome and does not claim to close the entire FT-000B card. Issue10 owns release admission/per-target publication; native runtime12, sonic-seed13, packaging14 and corpus ingestion11 stay separate. No source tests, runtime/device/media/provider operation, workflow/pin/configuration, secret, setting, assignment or operational board transition occurred.\n\nThis new independent worktree is stacked on owned synchronization PR1 full head/base `04e5ed3166941ff59b8f823d61465b9b015e8626`, preserving accepted upstream `a731093b878f600ee30648a01f1a6cd44f3439f0`. Personal PR2's sonic-seed plan remains unchanged. Development publication stays in the personal fork; final origin integration requires separately qualified release/deploy evidence.\n\nIndependent root peer review passed exact candidate `ef1885c16950355ffaf9e640189004f0aa9a24e4`: all1,534 unrelated synchronization-base blobs, three append-only prefixes and original event ledger are exact; all22 decoded native capture streams match size/SHA/raw bytes; actual current Receipt River API validates both new schema-declared rows75–76 at the full head; source is clean and cumulative diff hygiene passes. This is local preparation, not native approval or completed-review credit. Native planning qualification, the human-owned dependency and lawful Rheos readiness remain held. Automatic merge is off; manual reviewer requests are held for coordinator capacity/dedup checks.\n",
