    "number": 2,
    "title": "docs: refine portable sonic-seed planning",
    "body": "The existing incoming issue13 story describes portable sonic-seed tooling but leaves allocation bounds, canonical byte identity, runtime parity and implementation proof underspecified. This PR refines that same card and adds a planning contract against accepted current Calliope main, preserving its UUID, incoming state, five-point estimate, original acceptance scope, comments and event history.\n\nThe proposal defines shared pure contracts/domain/encoding, small NBB/Babashka adapters, bounded requests and frame budgets, deterministic EDN/MIDI/WAV/receipt artifacts, verified immutable reuse/conflicts, runtime parity, failure propagation and future red/green/hosted proof. Its full inherited burden is provisionally estimated at eight points: 3 semantic contracts/identity, 3 byte realization/immutable boundaries and 2 source CLI/skill/hosted proof. Planning review must justify retaining five or approve lawful Rheos breakdown; no children or dependency IDs are invented.\n\nThis contains no implementation. Provider calls, corpus ingestion, media hydration, native playback, packaged runtimes, release publication and issues11/12/14 are separate scopes. Historical unmerged PR8 remains source evidence, not merge qualification.\n\nIndependent review found no actionable issue in this proposal. Actual Rheos readback remains incoming/5pt and 37 cards/zero ready; frontmatter, comments and event bytes are unchanged. Original receipt prefixes, all native capture hashes, accepted source ancestry and full diff hygiene pass. Application tests and audio/parity results remain future requirements. Native planning qualification and a lawful ready transition are required before implementation. Automatic merge remains off.\n\nThis new private worktree stacks on the separate personal synchronization branch at `04e5ed3166941ff59b8f823d61465b9b015e8626`. Development stays on the personal fork; final integration is a qualified release/deploy PR into origin.\n",
