    "title": "chore: synchronize accepted Calliope history",
    "body": "The personal fork is five accepted commits behind origin and has no fork-only commits. This PR preserves accepted `octave-commons/calliope:main` at `a731093b878f600ee30648a01f1a6cd44f3439f0` as an ancestor and adds synchronization evidence, an append-only receipt and reflection. The upstream change advances the pinned MiMo review caller and binds its exact PR head; original workflow and receipt history are retained.\n\nIndependent inspection verified both personal and origin ancestry, original receipt prefixes, every capture hash, unchanged Rheos event bytes and full diff hygiene. The accepted workflow tree has no eager merge, deployment or release caller. No application code changes or application-test pass is claimed. Native review and current checks remain required; automatic merge stays off. This synchronization does not admit cards or activate a release controller.\n\nPrepared in a new private clone/worktree. Sonic-seed planning will be a separate development PR stacked on this exact branch. Final integration belongs in a qualified release/deploy PR into origin; this accepted-history synchronization is terminal intake, not deployment proof.\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **Chores**\n  * Updated pull request review checks to use the exact revision being reviewed.\n  * Added records and verification materials for a prepared upstream synchronization. The preparation preserves existing upstream history and leaves board state unchanged.\n* **Documentation**\n  * Added guidance and captured evidence for reviewing the synchronization candidate. Review and invitations remain pending, and automatic merging remains off.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->",
